Z||000002||mrfiero||12-09-2001||02:53 PM||||Bad plug wires are a common source of missing on '87-'88 DIS 4-cylinders.  <P>Some other possibilities are:<P>-bad coil packs<BR>-bad ignition module<BR>-bad crank sensor<BR>-fouled injector<P><BR>How bad of a miss do you have?  I used to have an '87 coupe and it missed something terrible......I found a plug wire with a crack in it which caused it to ground to the block.  <P>Change the plugs and wires and let us know what happens.||||reg||1
